load @term/seed/code/structure/set
  find set

# A function: a map that assigns to each element of one set (the domain) exactly one element of another (the codomain).
# It is the second pillar of the foundation after the set, the way structures are compared and built. A function may be
# injective (distinct inputs give distinct outputs), surjective (every output is reached), or bijective (both, a perfect
# pairing). Composition chains functions, and the identity function leaves its input unchanged. The form carries the
# domain and codomain sets; the single-valued assignment is the defining law.
form function
  link domain, like set
  link codomain, like set
